@Bijoun et al
PSATs are recommended for Juniors, not least because those scores were used by the National Merit folk to name the Scholars.  (I admit it's been quite some years now, but both our kids made that list.  It generated massive amounts of mail from colleges and universities.  )

There was also a big push for 8th-graders to take the exams, based (I think) on the supposition that it would boost later scores.  (It also promised those who fell for it --and paid the fees-- that they would be on mailing lists, etc., for the rest of their years in high school.)  Quite the money-maker for the ETS, eh?

