When I owned a chocolate shop, I bought quite a lot of strawberries every February. This is not strawberry season. I learned to pay extra for Driscoll's because they were reliably good (not great). The company has done a good job with their mission. There are other brands that can be excellent, but they weren't reliable. I'm glad I don't have to compete in that market.

Strawberries in France are so much better. I'm not sure if they are in supermarkets year round. The berries in the markets are seasonal and delicious.

