@lucky13
Not in a drought. I’ve lost all my blueberry plants and raspberry canes for the second Summer in a row. So depressing. We’re surrounded by orchards of apple, pear and plum. None of them have/will have produced anything like a decent harvest this year, it’s quite disheartening to look out at all the wilting trees.

I wish you joy of your garden and feel quite jealous. Thank goodness we had a bumper Strawberry crop before the rains dried up. The rain/Sun combo this Spring produced gorgeous, large sweet fruit. Am living on the memory.

